section('6. Proposed Work Schedule and Dependencies')
story += [P('The schedule is a planning baseline of seventeen working days, beginning on the team-selected start date. Working days exclude non-working periods selected by the group. They are not calendar dates or official submission deadlines. Parallel work assumes sufficient members and test resources; the coordinator must adjust it to actual capacity.'),T([['Card / activity','Working days','Dependency and planned output']]+[[c+' '+name,days,dep+'. Output: '+output+'.'] for c,name,days,dep,output in schedule],[145,62,268]),H('6.1 Dependency and capacity rules'),P('Cards 1 and 2 may be drafted concurrently but must be jointly reviewed before execution. Prepare accounts needed for imports before Card 5. Card 6 may start after a validated subset of Card 5 data is available. Card 7 requires the approved academic baseline; Card 8 requires complete assessment/source fixtures. Card 9 starts available dashboard checks early and completes downstream reporting after Card 8.'),P('Card 10 runs throughout execution for early triage and fixing. Days 13-15 are reserved for final fix verification and affected regression. Do not assign one member overlapping tasks beyond their capacity. A delayed prerequisite moves dependent dates; it must not be bypassed to preserve the original calendar.')]

section('7. Calendar Commitments and Milestones')
story += [P('Enter real calendar dates in YYYY-MM-DD format and copy them to each Trello card\'s Dates field. Use actual member names under Members. These editable fields define the committed calendar once reviewed; an empty field is not an assigned deadline.'),Field('calendar_anchor','Start date / Capstone milestone / assessment submission deadline'),Calendar([(1,'Requirements review'),(2,'Test plan and schedule'),(3,'Cases and fixtures'),(4,'Accounts/access'),(5,'Classes/uploads'),(6,'Grades/attendance'),(7,'Referrals/assessment'),(8,'Prediction/routing'),(9,'Dashboards/quality'),(10,'Fixes/regression'),(11,'Final review'),(12,'Presentation/submission')]),Spacer(1,9),H('7.1 Milestone acceptance'),small('Working day 2: requirements and test plan reviewed. Day 4: cases/environment ready. Day 12: initial execution recorded, including blocked/not-run cases. Day 15: fixes/retesting/regression reviewed. Day 16: readiness decision recorded. Day 17: board checked and each member submits the required link and screenshot.'),Field('calendar_review','Calendar reviewed by / review date / approved adjustments',35)]

section('8. Entry, Exit, Suspension and Resumption Criteria')
story += [H('8.1 Entry criteria'),P('Begin a test only when its expected behavior is reviewed, required accounts/fixtures exist, the selected build is reachable, evidence capture works and the environment is isolated from production. Resolve requirements findings affecting the expected outcome or explicitly record the case as Blocked. Confirm prerequisites separately for each prediction entry point.'),H('8.2 Test and task completion'),P('A case passes only when all expected conditions are observed with reproducible evidence. A task card may be completed when its agreed execution/reporting output is reviewed, even if product defects remain open on linked cards. This does not approve the system. Card checklists and dates must reflect actual work.'),H('8.3 Proposed overall QA exit criteria'),T([['Criterion','Required evidence'],['Coverage accounted for','All scoped cases and supplemental scenarios classified as Pass, Fail, Blocked or Not run, with reasons for exclusions.'],['Core workflows verified','Access/ownership, import integrity, academic calculations and core intervention flow pass on the reviewed build.'],['Release blockers controlled','No unresolved Critical/High defect compromising private data, academic integrity or a core intervention function. If one remains, record Not ready.'],['Fixes independently checked','Original failures and affected regressions rerun; reopening and limitations recorded.'],['Quality and residual risks reviewed','Approved targets assessed; model limitations disclosed; lower-severity residual issues accepted by a named authorized reviewer.'],['Final decision recorded','QA summary, build, reviewers, date and rationale present; no implied or fabricated approval.']],[150,325]),H('8.4 Suspend and resume'),P('Suspend affected tests for database instability, incorrect fixtures, unavailable essential services, unsafe real-data exposure, invalid build identity or a blocker preventing meaningful observation. Preserve logs and mark the affected tests Blocked. Resume after the cause is corrected, the environment is rechecked, scope is reassessed and impacted earlier tests are selected for regression.'),P('Submission readiness and product readiness are separate decisions. The group may submit an accurate board showing unresolved work; it must not relabel failures or invent approvals to meet the submission date.')]

section('9. Defects, Metrics and Quality Measurement')
story += [H('9.1 Defect lifecycle'),P('Create a linked BUG record containing case/requirement, build, steps, expected and actual outcomes, impact, evidence, severity, priority, developer and target date. Workflow: Open, In progress, Fixed awaiting verification, Verified or Reopened. An accepted limitation remains a documented residual issue, not a verified fix.'),T([['Severity','Impact definition'],['Critical','Private-data exposure, major data loss/corruption or total core service failure.'],['High','Incorrect or unavailable core function without an acceptable workaround.'],['Medium','Partial failure with an available workaround or limited scope.'],['Low','Minor presentation or wording issue without material functional impact.']],[90,385]),H('9.2 Execution metrics'),P('Planned = Pass + Fail + Blocked + Not run, using one consistent scenario-counting unit. Executed = Pass + Fail. Execution rate = Executed / Planned x 100. Pass rate among executed = Pass / Executed x 100. Use N/A when a denominator is zero. Report failed, blocked and unexecuted coverage openly; do not convert it into passing coverage.'),H('9.3 Performance protocol and proposed targets'),P('Use a 100-student synthetic class, recorded device/network/browser/server conditions and a single-user baseline. Measure twenty runs per selected dashboard, search and single-student prediction task. Declare the timing boundary, distinguish cold from warm runs, and report median and nearest-rank p95 together with errors/timeouts. Sort twenty observed durations; nearest-rank p95 is the nineteenth duration.'),P('Proposed acceptance: p95 dashboard/search at or below 3 seconds and p95 single-student prediction at or below 5 seconds. These limits require team approval before execution. Report cold-start observations separately and retain failures; do not replace failed requests with zero durations. Record upload size/rows and duration separately.'),Field('quality_targets','Approved targets / workload changes / approver and date',40),H('9.4 Usability and model outcomes'),P('Document defined task completion, confusing steps, keyboard/focus behavior, validation clarity and viewport coverage. Do not invent satisfaction ratings. Model evidence follows Section 3.2; no accuracy threshold is assumed without an approved requirement.')]

section('10. Evidence, Deliverables and Trello Monitoring')
story += [T([['Card','Planned attachment / evidence'],['1','Academic Requirements Review Report and actual review dispositions'],['2','This Test Plan and Schedule with actual assignments/dates'],['3','AEWS_Test_Cases.xlsx with reviewed procedures and scenario extensions'],['4','Account/access results including student/admin checks; actual screenshots'],['5','Class/upload results and synthetic valid/negative fixture files'],['6','Grade/attendance reconciliation workbook; actual evidence'],['7','Referral/assessment results and relevant form evidence'],['8','Prediction/routing results and model evaluation record'],['9','Dashboard/quality results, export validation record and actual system export'],['10','Bug/retest register and end-to-end regression record'],['11','Final QA summary and actual readiness decision'],['12','Presentation script, actual readable board screenshots and submission checks']],[45,430]),H('10.1 Evidence management'),P('Use filenames identifying the case, build and date, for example TC-19-A_referral_boundary_buildID_date.png. Record the unmodified expectation separately from observed results. Store sensitive originals privately if required; publish only synthetic or sanitized evidence. Keep logs free of passwords, tokens, connection strings and confidential student information [1].'),H('10.2 Board operation'),P('Use Backlog, To Do, In Progress, Testing and Completed. Assign actual Members and Dates. Use category labels, genuine progress comments, linked defects and useful attachments. A reviewer checks the output before completion. Mark dependency delays in comments and revise affected dates.'),H('10.3 Presentation and submission'),P('Explain the structure, owners, deadlines, QA choices and actual status using one representative detailed card. Each member individually submits the shared public board link and readable screenshot as required by the activity. Verify signed-out access only after removing sensitive content [1-2].')]

section('11. Risks, Change Control and Plan Approval')
story += [T([['Risk','Response and accountable function'],['Requirements remain ambiguous','QA coordinator obtains decisions; block affected expected outcomes and update traceability.'],['Incorrect academic mapping','Academic-data tester reconciles source identities/terms before downstream tests.'],['Private-data or role leakage','Access tester prioritizes isolation checks; suspend unsafe affected workflows and record blocker.'],['Prediction appears valid with missing data','AMU/model tester verifies sources, output meaning and model/fallback provenance.'],['Service/email/model unavailable','Environment owner uses controlled services, documents blocked cases and restores prerequisites.'],['Schedule overruns or fix regressions','Coordinator reserves retest days, triages daily and rebaselines dependencies honestly.']],[155,320]),H('11.1 Change control'),P('Record changes to scope, requirements, cases, targets, owners, environment or dates with a reason, affected IDs, reviewer and decision date. Reassess dependencies and regression needs. Retain previous versions and execution history; do not overwrite failed evidence with a later pass.'),H('11.2 Actual review and approval'),Field('team_prepared','Team / prepared by'),Field('plan_reviewer','Plan reviewer(s) and roles'),Field('plan_decision','Decision: approve / approve with conditions / revise and resubmit'),Field('plan_conditions','Conditions, approved changes and unresolved dependencies',45),Field('approval_date','Actual acknowledgement / review date / approved plan version'),small('The plan is not approved until the project reviewers record their actual decision. This acknowledgement does not imply an instructor signature or approval.')]

section('12. References and Planning Basis')
refs=[('[1]','Bukidnon State University, College of Technologies, Information Technology Department. (n.d.). IT143 CO3 major assessment guidelines: Quality Assurance Project Management Framework using Trello. Supplied PDF, pp. 1-3.'),('[2]','Bukidnon State University, College of Technologies. (n.d.). Rubric for group activity using Trello: Quality Assurance Project Management Framework/timeline creation. Supplied PDF, p. 1.'),('[3]','AEWS project group. (2026). Requirements Review Report (AEWS-QA-RR-001, version 2.0). Requirement groups R01-R17 and review findings F01-F07. Static review; stakeholder validation pending.'),('[4]','AEWS QA preparation materials. (2026). AEWS_Test_Cases.xlsx, TC-01 to TC-40, and card-specific result/evidence templates. Prepared procedures; not evidence that tests have been executed.'),('[5]','AEWS project repository. (n.d.). README.md; frontend/package.json; frontend/src/App.jsx; backend/app/authz.py; backend/app/main.py; backend/app/routers/classes.py, students.py, amu_staff.py and admin.py. Local project artifacts used to establish scope and candidate test paths.'),('[6]','AEWS project repository. (n.d.). backend/app/ai_model.py; backend/MODEL_DOCUMENTATION.md; backend/tests/test_amu_prediction_requirements.py. Prediction source, model documentation and existing prerequisite tests. Their presence does not establish passing runtime behavior.')]
